  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A$ be a $3 \\times 3$ matrix such that<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& |\\operatorname{adj}(\\operatorname{adj}(\\operatorname{adj} \\mathrm{A}))|=81 . \\text { If } \\\\\n& \\mathrm{S}=\\left\\{\\mathrm{n} \\in \\mathbb{Z}:(|\\operatorname{adj}(\\operatorname{adj} A)|)^{\\frac{(n-1)^2}{2}}=|A|^{\\left(3 n^2-5 n-4\\right)}\\right\\}<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>, then $\\sum_{n \\in S}\\left|A^{\\left(n^2+n\\right)}\\right|$ is equal to"
  },
